    "1.1.0": "MAJOR CRYPTOGRAPHIC ENHANCEMENT: Extended hash algorithm support with complete SHA-2 family (SHA-224/384) and SHA-3 family (SHA3-224/384), added BLAKE3 ultra-fast hashing and SHAKE-128 extendable-output function. Implemented RFC 5869 HKDF key derivation with configurable hash algorithms and iteration rounds. Added comprehensive post-quantum signature support with MAYO-1/3/5 multivariate and CROSS-128/192/256 code-based algorithms. Complete GUI redesign with professional hash family organization (SHA-2, SHA-3, BLAKE, SHAKE, Legacy) and dedicated KDF Algorithm Settings section. Enhanced CLI with full coverage of all hash algorithms and HKDF configuration options. Improved security posture by reclassifying PBKDF2 as legacy KDF (disabled by default). Now includes enhanced Flutter GUI with configuration profiles, security improvements, and input validation backported from latest development. Extensive testing infrastructure with 93+ CLI parameter validation, dual implementation consistency testing, removal of deprecated pqc-allow-mixed-operations parameter, and systematic cleanup of 63 development artifacts. Comprehensive documentation updates reflecting modern vs. legacy algorithm categorization.",
    "1.2.0": "PROFESSIONAL FLUTTER DESKTOP & SECURITY HARDENING: Complete migration from tkinter to Flutter desktop providing native Wayland and X11 support, advanced CLI integration with real-time progress monitoring, comprehensive settings system with theme switching and cryptographic defaults. Desktop UX excellence with menu bar, keyboard shortcuts, drag & drop file operations, NavigationRail sidebar, tabbed interface, and algorithm recommendation engine with security guidance. Added advanced algorithm configuration UI for all KDFs (Argon2, Scrypt, Balloon, HKDF) and post-quantum algorithms (ML-KEM, Kyber, HQC, MAYO, CROSS). Enhanced security through cryptographic hardening: permanently removed deprecated PBKDF2 key derivation and Whirlpool hash algorithms from new encryption operations (existing encrypted files with these algorithms can still be decrypted). Now includes enhanced Flutter GUI with configuration profiles, security improvements, and input validation backported from latest development. Streamlined Flatpak architecture removing complex X11/XWayland compatibility layers. Professional desktop integration with native dialogs and comprehensive JSON schema validation system for keystore and metadata structures.",
    "1.2.1": "Documentation maintenance release: Minor updates to documentation, user guides, and help text to improve clarity and user experience. Now includes enhanced Flutter GUI with configuration profiles, security improvements, and input validation backported from latest development. No functional changes to cryptographic operations or core features.",
    "1.3.0": "CRYPTOGRAPHIC ENHANCEMENT & BUG FIXES: Added RandomX proof-of-work key derivation function optimized for CPUs with light (256MB) and fast (2GB) modes. Fixed critical default configuration decryption failure caused by metadata generation inconsistency between PBKDF2 parameter defaults and security template settings. Resolved post-quantum cryptography dual encryption test failures through improved test data parsing with binary prefix handling. Enhanced Docker build optimization reducing image size to 140MB with proper runtime library dependencies. Implemented comprehensive debug logging system replacing print statements. Added security enhancements: automatic application of default hash/KDF configuration when none specified to prevent direct password encryption, and security warnings when KDFs would operate directly on user password without sufficient entropy from prior hashing. Maintained full backward compatibility for all existing encrypted files while improving new encryption consistency. Now includes enhanced Flutter GUI with configuration profiles, security improvements, and input validation backported from latest development.",
    "1.3.1": "SECURITY & MAINTENANCE: Critical HSM security fix removing --device=all from Flatpak manifest, requiring explicit USB device opt-in for hardware security modules. Fixed post-quantum private key storage for AEAD algorithms. Enhanced Flatpak permissions with explicit Yubikey/smart card device access. Cleaned up Flatpak manifest removing invalid filesystem permissions.",
    "1.3.2": "SECURITY & PERFORMANCE MONITORING: Implemented comprehensive decryption time/memory estimation system to prevent DoS attacks via inflated metadata parameters. Added static benchmark data for all hash algorithms (SHA-224/256/384/512, SHA3-224/256/384/512, BLAKE2b/3, SHAKE-128/256) and KDF operations (PBKDF2, Argon2, Scrypt, Balloon, HKDF, RandomX). Pre-decryption cost display shows operation breakdown with conservative estimates, warns when thresholds exceeded (>10 seconds or >1GB memory), and provides 2-second cancellation window. Added --no-estimate CLI flag to suppress display for trusted files. Fixed critical argument parsing bug where --no-estimate failed when used with --progress flag due to preprocessor moving global flags before subcommand detection. Enhanced CLI robustness with improved subcommand detection after global flag preprocessing. Benchmarking system uses empirically validated non-linear scaling for memory-hard KDFs (Balloon: space_cost^0.85, Scrypt: exponential doubling). All existing encrypted files maintain full backward compatibility. Now includes enhanced Flutter GUI with configuration profiles, security improvements, and input validation backported from latest development.",
    "1.3.3": "LICENSE COMPLIANCE: Updated license declaration from MIT to Hippocratic License 3.0 across all distribution channels (PyPI, Flatpak). Fixed Flatpak metainfo.xml project_license field and added explicit license field to setup.py. No functional changes to cryptographic operations or features. Repository-wide license standardization for proper compliance.",
    "1.3.4": "CRITICAL SECURITY FIX (CVSSv3 8.1 HIGH): Fixed predictable salt derivation vulnerability (CWE-330) in multi-round KDF operations. Implemented Format Version 7 with secure chained salt derivation where each round uses previous round output as salt, preventing precomputation attacks. Affects all multi-round operations: BLAKE2b, BLAKE3, SHAKE-256, Argon2, Scrypt, Balloon, PBKDF2, HKDF. Full backward compatibility for decrypting Format Versions 3-6. Files encrypted with v1.3.4+ require v1.3.4 or newer to decrypt.",
    "1.3.5": "BLAKE3 HASH INTEGRATION: Added BLAKE3 keyed hashing support with 32-byte keys for format_version 7. Implemented BLAKE3-aware buffer sizing (64 bytes minimum) for proper key derivation with zero-initialization for deterministic hashing. Enhanced BLAKE3 detection in both flat (v3) and nested (v4+) hash config formats. Added comprehensive debug logging for BLAKE3 operations. Included build scripts for liboqs dependencies and Flatpak CI jobs. Fully backward compatible with v1.3.0-1.3.4 encrypted files and cross-version compatible with v1.4.x.",
    "1.4.0": "POST-QUANTUM ASYMMETRIC ENCRYPTION: Major release introducing Format Version 7 with post-quantum asymmetric encryption capabilities. Added ML-KEM-768 (Kyber) for key encapsulation and ML-DSA-65 (Dilithium) for digital signatures, providing quantum-resistant security. Implemented comprehensive Identity Management System with dual keypairs (encryption + signing), private key encryption at rest (Argon2id + AES-256-GCM), and identity storage in ~/.openssl_encrypt/identities/. Added multiple recipients support allowing single file encryption for N recipients with minimal overhead (~1.2KB per recipient). Implemented DoS Protection via signature verification before expensive KDF operations (fast ~1-5ms signature check prevents KDF attacks). Added complete Identity CLI with 7 commands (create, list, show, export, import, delete, change-password) for identity lifecycle management. Enhanced asymmetric encryption CLI with --for (multiple recipients), --sign-with (sender identity), --key (recipient for decryption), --verify-from (signature verification), and --no-verify flags. Integrated HSM Plugin Support with YubiKey Challenge-Response and plugin system architecture. Added benchmarking system for performance analysis and decryption time estimator for progress feedback. Comprehensive security enhancements: secure memory management (CryptoKey class, SecureBytes, secure_memzero), metadata integrity via digital signatures over canonical metadata, defense in depth with KDF chain running even in asymmetric mode. New modules: pqc_signing.py (450 lines), identity.py (750 lines), asymmetric_core.py (650 lines), identity_cli.py (540 lines). Extended modules: crypt_core.py (+700 lines), pqc.py (+100 lines). Added 120 new tests covering all asymmetric features with zero warnings. Format V7 maintains full backward compatibility with V6 symmetric encryption. No new dependencies (uses existing cryptography, argon2-cffi, liboqs-python). Production-ready with comprehensive documentation (ASYMMETRIC_ENCRYPTION_GUIDE.md), full test coverage, and security audit.",
    "1.4.0b8": "CRITICAL SECURITY FIX (BETA): Implemented Format Version 9 with secure chained salt derivation, resolving predictable salt issue in v1.4.x branch. Unified security model where v7 and v9 use secure chained derivation (unpredictable), v8 uses predictable derivation (backward compatibility only). Fixed critical pepper plugin scoping errors causing 100+ test failures. Added comprehensive Flatpak CI/CD pipeline with build and publish stages. Enhanced Flutter GUI with remote pepper plugin integration, integrity verification, cascade encryption UI, asymmetric encryption configuration, and YubiKey touch prompt improvements. Fixed HSM plugin loading and dependency management. Beta release addressing security vulnerability discovered in earlier v1.4.0 betas.",
    "1.4.0b9": "STABILITY & COMPATIBILITY (BETA): Test infrastructure improvements and cross-version compatibility fixes. Fixed 6 salt derivation test failures by correcting test suite to use generate_key() instead of multi_hash_password() for KDF operations. Completed Threefish-512/1024 cipher support with HKDF key expansion and proper AEAD integration. Fixed BLAKE3 buffer sizing for backward compatibility with pre-BLAKE3 encrypted files. Fixed critical metadata v7 schema compatibility with v1.3.4 (made 'mode' field optional). Resolved Scrypt bytearray conversion issues and XChaCha20 SecureBytes slice handling. Enhanced debug logging for version-aware salt derivation decisions. Full test suite: 1535 tests passing, 0 failures. Format Version 9 security model validated across all KDF algorithms (PBKDF2, Argon2, Scrypt, Balloon).",
    "1.4.0b10": "INDEPENDENT XOR & PARALLEL PROCESSING (BETA): Implemented Format Version 11 with Massey's Independent XOR composition providing 'strongest component' security guarantee where key remains secure even if all algorithms except the strongest are broken. Added optional parallel KDF processing with ~2.7x performance improvement (8.5s → 3.1s with 8 algorithms on 8-core CPU) using ProcessPoolExecutor for true CPU parallelism. New CLI flags: --independent-xor enables v11 format, --parallel-kdf enables parallel processing (requires --independent-xor), --kdf-workers N specifies worker count (default: auto-detect). Added comprehensive parallel_kdf.py module (739 lines) with Queue-based progress aggregation and GUI integration. Enhanced decrypt path with format version 11 support in 5 key locations. Added metadata_v11_schema.json with xor_mode field to distinguish Independent XOR (v11) from Sequential XOR (v10). Includes 7 new v11 Independent XOR tests and 11 parallel KDF tests. Full test suite: 1573 tests passing (up from 1535). Cross-branch compatible with v9 format in 1.3.x branch for seamless migration.",
    "1.4.2": "DESKTOP GUI & CRYPTO DEFAULTS: Added Simple/Pro mode toggle for desktop GUI — Simple mode (default) hides all advanced crypto options and uses the STANDARD template automatically. Modernized STANDARD template: hashes updated to SHA3-512 + BLAKE3 (10k rounds each), KDFs changed to RandomX (10 rounds) + Argon2 (10 rounds), encryption upgraded to 2-layer cascade (AES-256-GCM + ChaCha20-Poly1305). Independent XOR (v11) now enabled by default for STANDARD and PARANOID templates. Added RandomX support to independent XOR key derivation path. Added progress bars for multi-round Argon2 and RandomX in XOR mode. Dependency bumps: cryptography 46.0.6, requests 2.33.0, black 26.3.1, nltk 3.9.4.",
    "1.4.3": "BUGFIX: Fixed Flutter GUI launcher in Flatpak — corrected binary name in wrapper script so --gui flag works correctly. Fixed GTK window title from 'openssl_encrypt_mobile' to 'OpenSSL Encrypt'.",
    "1.5.0": "SECURITY HARDENING, NEW TOOLING & CODE-SURFACE REDUCTION: Major release combining a security-review fix batch, new CLI capabilities and a ~28,000-line cleanup (-23% of production code). SECURITY: authenticated v2 keystore format with HMAC-SHA256 over the whole structure, failing closed on tampering, legacy keystores auto-upgrade on save (H4/M6); PQC algorithm resolution fails closed instead of silently downgrading to the weakest available KEM (H3); portable USB drives use a unique random per-drive KDF salt instead of a global fixed salt (H5); plugin sandbox enforces file/network/process restrictions on the default process-isolation path, closes the AST frame/traceback escape and rejects world-writable plugin locations (H8); Balloon KDF gets a persisted memory-hard default space_cost on the v11 path (M3); weak 10k-iteration PBKDF2 dual-encryption verifier no longer written to metadata (M7); identity layer gains TOFU key-change detection with IdentityKeyChangedError and full-fingerprint lookup (M8); secure_memzero reports honestly on immutable input and the KDF password wipe is effective and copy-free (M10/M10a); metadata schema validation registers schemas dynamically and fails closed on unknown format_version, activating the previously unregistered v9/v12 schemas (M11). Fixed a cascade + streaming per-chunk nonce reuse: streaming a cascade chain reused one cascade salt for every chunk, and since each cascade layer derives its key and AEAD nonce from (master_key, salt) this reused per-layer nonces across all chunks (catastrophic AEAD nonce reuse for multi-chunk cascade v12 files); each chunk now derives a unique cascade salt via HKDF (metadata streaming.cascade_nonce_scheme=2), legacy files are read as scheme 1 for backward compatibility and emit a security warning urging rekey, and non-cascade streaming was unaffected. FEATURES: real 192-bit XChaCha20-Poly1305 nonces per draft-irtf-cfrg-xchacha-03 (new modules/xchacha.py, metadata flag xchacha_nonce_format=2, auto-detected legacy decryption); 'info' action reconstructs the full encrypt CLI from file metadata including removed-algorithm migration hints; Diceware passphrase generation for generate-password (--dice, bundled EFF large wordlist, entropy reporting); derive-password gains HSM-aware deterministic derivation (--hsm/--hsm-slot) and --confirm; OnlyKey Challenge-Response HSM plugin with identity protection and cross-device deterministic pepper guarantee. FIXED: streaming data-loss bug where streaming files recorded the wrong format_version; pytest collection regression that silently skipped 91 tests in unittests.py since 2025-12-30. REMOVED (code-surface reduction): steganography subsystem (numpy dependency dropped; extract hidden data with v1.4.x before upgrading), D-Bus service/client, in-package security testing framework, advisory configuration tooling (config-wizard, analyze-config, analyze-security, template subcommand, smart-recommendations) and dead security_report.py. Encryption templates (-t/--template, --quick/--standard/--paranoid, custom JSON/YAML) work unchanged; decryption cost estimator retained as DoS protection; all plugins retained. Full backward compatibility: every decrypt path preserved - all files encrypted with earlier versions still decrypt. Test suite green through five staged removals (4602 tests passing, zero regressions). CROSS-DEVICE HSM: yubikey_hsm/onlykey_hsm now form a protocol-compatible family - files encrypted with one device decrypt with the other via explicit --hsm when both hold the same HMAC-SHA1 secret; --hsm-slot on decrypt/rekey overrides the metadata slot (previously printed but silently ignored). OnlyKey plugin fixed for real hardware (PID masquerade as OTP-only YubiKey, OtpConnection request, actionable challenge-rejection errors) and new ONLYKEY_SETUP.md guide (udev rules, unlock-then-touch flow, challenge-code caveat). threefish_native builds on Python 3.14 (PyO3 0.26). Declared Python floor raised to >=3.11, aligning metadata with the documented requirement and the 1.4.x line; 3.14 classifiers added. ASCII ARMOR: new encrypt --armor/-a flag writes PEM-style Base64 (ASCII-armored) output that is safe to paste into email, chat, YAML or a clipboard; the encrypted blob is wrapped in a BEGIN/END OPENSSL-ENCRYPT MESSAGE envelope with an OpenPGP-style CRC-24 checksum that detects paste truncation (fails closed on malformed armor). decrypt/info/verify auto-detect armored input by content (no flag needed) and the round-trip is byte-exact; works across the symmetric, stdin->stdout streaming and recipient/asymmetric output paths. New module modules/armor.py, covered by the signed integrity manifest. ENCRYPT-TO-SELF: when encrypting for recipients (--for-identity), the sender's own identity (--sign-with) is now added as an additional recipient by default so the sender can later decrypt their own outbound file (removing a common data-loss footgun); the sender slot reuses the existing multi-recipient ML-KEM wrapping and is de-duplicated by fingerprint. Opt out with --no-encrypt-to-self. DETACHED FILE SIGNING: new sign/verify-signature actions produce and verify a detached post-quantum (ML-DSA-65) signature over an arbitrary file, closing the authenticity gap of symmetric AEAD (where anyone who knows the password can forge a valid file). sign --input F --sign-with IDENTITY writes a .sig JSON sidecar (ASCII-armored by default, --no-armor for raw) binding the file's SHA-512 to the signer over a domain-separated payload distinct from the encrypted-file metadata signature. verify-signature resolves the signer's public key from the local identity store and contacts by the embedded fingerprint, fails closed on an unknown signer (--signer to pin), reports which component(s) verified, and supports --json. The sidecar signatures list is forward-compatible with a future classical hybrid component. New module modules/file_signature.py, covered by the signed integrity manifest. FOREIGN-FORMAT INTEROP (decrypt --from age): read-only decryption of age/rage files to ease migration. Supports X25519 recipients (--age-identity keys.txt) and scrypt passphrase files (age -p via --password), binary and ASCII-armored input, and skips unknown/GREASE stanzas. Implemented directly on pyca cryptography (no new dependency) and validated against the age reference implementation's known-answer vectors. Untrusted-input hardening: header MAC and every payload chunk authenticated before any plaintext is returned, scrypt must be the only stanza, work factor capped, bounded reads. New package modules/interop/. Also adds OpenPGP symmetric decryption (decrypt --from pgp): passphrase-based gpg -c messages parsed directly on pyca (no GnuPG dependency) - SKESK + S2K, SEIPD v1 (CFB + SHA-1 MDC), inner ZIP/ZLIB/BZIP2 compression, ciphers 3DES/CAST5/AES/Camellia, validated against real GnuPG output. The unauthenticated SED packet is refused and decompression/packet sizes are bounded. OpenPGP public-key messages are also supported (decrypt --from pgp --pgp-key FILE): parses an exported secret key (unlocked with the key passphrase) and unwraps the session key for RSA (PKCS#1 v1.5) and ECDH (RFC 6637 KDF + RFC 3394 key-wrap) over Curve25519 and NIST P-256/384/521, validated against real GnuPG keypairs. ENVELOPE ENCRYPTION (DEK/KEK): new opt-in --envelope mode encrypts bulk data under a random Data Encryption Key (DEK) and wraps that DEK with a Key Encryption Key derived from the password through the full unchanged KDF chain (stored as encryption.wrapped_dek; decryption auto-detects). Enables O(header) credential rekey - changing the password rewraps the small DEK and rewrites only the metadata header, retaining the bulk ciphertext verbatim instead of re-encrypting it (this rotates the access credential, not the data key; full re-encrypt remains available for true data-key rotation). The bulk AEAD binds a canonical stable subset of the metadata that excludes only the KEK-gating fields a rekey changes (KDF salt/config + wrapped_dek), so a rekey keeps the ciphertext valid while tampering any authenticated field still fails closed. For a cascade chain the DEK is wrapped under the SAME chain (not single AES-256-GCM) so the envelope is never weaker than the payload. Opt-in and fully backward-compatible: non-envelope files are byte-for-byte unchanged and keep full-metadata binding; DEK/KEK are zeroed on every path and never logged. Foundation for future multi-password/multi-recipient wrapping. Fixed a pre-release cross-version envelope bug: a 1.4.x file using --envelope with a cascade chain containing xchacha20-poly1305 could not be decrypted after upgrading to 1.5.x - 1.4.x wraps the DEK with the legacy 12-byte XChaCha nonce and writes no xchacha_nonce_format flag, but the envelope DEK-unwrap hardcoded the new 192-bit format (xchacha_nonce_format=2), so the DEK never authenticated and the file was permanently unreadable (the break was unique to envelope+xchacha; the bulk cascade path already defaulted an absent flag to legacy 1, so plain cascade+xchacha and single xchacha always interoperated); the DEK wrap/unwrap now honor the file's xchacha_nonce_format (absent => legacy 1) on both the decrypt and rekey paths, newly written 1.5.x files are unchanged and still use the real 192-bit construction, and a committed genuine 1.4.x vector guards the path. SECURITY REVIEW FOLLOW-UP (2026-07-07, each fixed with a regression test and crypto-reviewer sign-off): H1 [HSM-1] the hsm fido2-test command printed the full 32-byte derived hardware pepper as hex to stdout unconditionally, outside the debug_secret() redaction chokepoint — the hex dump is removed (length still reported). M1 [PLUGIN-2] the plugin loader verified a signature over one read while AST-scanning and executing others (verify-A/execute-B) and could exec a cached .pyc never covered by the signature — _validate_plugin_file now reads the plugin once as raw bytes threaded through the signature gate, the sha256(raw) pin and ast.parse(raw), and load_plugin re-reads once, compares to the pin, and executes via compile(raw)+exec instead of spec.loader.exec_module, killing the CRLF/BOM and .pyc-shadow discrepancies (fail-closed on a missing pin for non-built-ins). H2 [PLUGIN-1] a package plugin signed only its __init__.py while transitively importing unverified sibling modules (a signed __init__.py plus a malicious unsigned helper.py executed unchecked) — a signed per-package PLUGIN.manifest with one detached PLUGIN.manifest.asc now covers every importable module (source .py, bytecode .pyc, native .so/.pyd, recursively including underscore-prefixed and nested), verified via the existing trust anchors plus an exact on-disk tree match with every module hash-pinned and every source sibling AST-scanned; under enforce a tampered/unlisted/native-swapped/impostor-signed sibling is refused, warn warns and loads, built-in packages keep the trust shortcut; plugin sign auto-detects a package and writes the manifest (a runtime import-hook for the validation-to-import TOCTOU window remains a documented follow-on). M2 [MEM-1] several callers wrapped an immutable bytes secret in bytearray(...) and called secure_memzero on the throwaway copy (a no-op wipe) in parallel_kdf.py, asymmetric_core.py, pqc.py and crypt_core.py — each secret is now held in a bytearray/SecureBytes from creation and that object is wiped. M3 [KDF-1] the parallel and sequential Independent-XOR paths derived different keys for Argon2 rounds greater than 1 — the parallel worker now matches the sequential derivation exactly. R1 [KDF-2b] a RandomX failure in the parallel Independent-XOR path was swallowed (fail-open) unlike the sequential path — both now fail closed. M4 [STREAM-1] a streaming per-chunk AEAD authentication failure was classified by substring-matching the exception text — classification is now structural. LEGACY KEM DECRYPT RETRY: PQC files written by 1.4.x releases up to 1.4.7 used a bare-SHA256 KEM key at format versions 12/13 and could not be decrypted on this line; an authenticated one-shot legacy retry now reads them (the AEAD tag rejects wrong keys, so no downgrade surface) with a re-encryption notice. EMBEDDED PQC KEY FIX: v11-v13 files with an embedded password-encrypted post-quantum private key always failed to decrypt (Missing PQC key salt) because the salt lookup was gated on format versions 4-10 — the gate now covers every v4+ format, with regression round-trips. FORMAT VERSION 14 GROUNDWORK (not yet the default): new independent-XOR-only format version 14 with fail-closed guards (no v14 sequential-XOR file can exist, unknown future versions are refused even without the schema validator). V14 TLV KDF SEED: format version 14 seeds the independent-XOR derivation from length-prefixed password/salt/pepper fields instead of raw concatenation (finding #100 boundary ambiguity), pinned for cross-line byte-identity; everything below v14 derives byte-identically. V14 KEM TRANSCRIPT BINDING: v14 PQC files bind the KEM symmetric key to the full transcript (algorithm, AEAD choice and a digest of the KEM encapsulation ciphertext) via HKDF-SHA256, with the legacy decrypt retry scoped to v12/v13 only. FORMAT VERSION 14 IS NOW THE DEFAULT WRITE FORMAT: new encryptions (including streaming) default to the independent-XOR robust-combiner topology, wide keys (AES-SIV, Threefish) derive at full length on every v14 path, sequential XOR remains a supported opt-in pinned at format version 13, explicit version requests are honored, and every existing file decrypts unchanged. STREAMING + SEQUENTIAL-XOR DATA-LOSS FIX: that combination silently wrote files that always failed chunk authentication on decrypt; it is now refused with a clear error pointing to --no-streaming. KEYSTORE VERSION-GATE FIX: keystore dual-encryption metadata lookups were gated on format versions 4-10, failing for v11+ files — the gates now cover every v4+ format. RANDOMX WIDE-KEY FIX: RandomX-enabled configs crashed key derivation for AES-SIV/Threefish (the 32-byte RandomX output is now HKDF-normalized to the full key length; 32-byte-key files are unaffected). REMOVED-PBKDF2 MIGRATION ERROR: decrypting a 1.4.x sequential file that used the removed PBKDF2 chain stage now fails up front with guidance naming the breaking change and the migration path (decrypt with 1.4.x, re-encrypt) instead of a generic authentication error; independent-XOR files carrying the same metadata entry keep decrypting. V14 REVIEW REMEDIATIONS (crypto-reviewer pass 2026-07-10, two Low findings): the v14 TLV KDF seed is hashed through a memoryview instead of an immutable bytes copy, so no unwipeable copy of the cleartext password/salt/pepper is materialized (M2 [MEM-1] hygiene; derived keys byte-identical per the cross-line golden vectors), and the KEM transcript-binding documentation now states that ciphertext/metadata substitution is detected via AEAD authentication (wrong key fails the tag), so the PQC symmetric layer must remain an AEAD (all reachable PQC data ciphers are AEADs, including Threefish via CTR+Poly1305). V14 SEED ENCODER SINGLE-ALLOCATION (post-v14 review LOW-1, 2026-07-11): the v14 TLV KDF seed was built with incremental bytearray growth, so CPython reallocations could leave partial copies of the length-prefixed cleartext password in freed unwiped heap (the final secure_memzero wipes only the last allocation) and the bytes() field conversion materialized an unwipeable copy of mutable secrets — the seed is now written into one exact-size preallocated bytearray through memoryviews (no reallocation, no immutable copies; M2 [MEM-1] hygiene); not exploitable on its own, derived keys and the on-disk format are byte-identical (cross-line golden vectors plus a new byte-identity test matrix). KEYSTORE VERSION-GATE TYPE SAFETY (post-v14 review LOW-2, 2026-07-11): the keystore integration read format_version from raw parsed JSON and compared it with >=, so a crafted file carrying a non-int val